N:THE PLATE: "Allegro", 2/4, no key signature, three staves with a repeat; words "Ra-na dji-nak, Ya dou-aï-ni, Ra-na dji-nak, Na-ri! Ya na-ri!" Below, "Rythme d'accompagnement": two lines of strokes, the upper (high) and lower (low), "etc."
N:HOW READ (2026-11-10): p. 2824 from the archive.org scan (about 190 dpi, staff lines 16.5 pixels apart); the staff lines found by row darkness and found again beside each note, since the page is slightly skewed; each filled head measured against those local lines (all within 0.4 of a step but one, read by eye); the hollow half notes and the rhythm read on enlargements; every bar checked to make two quarters. Words placed as Rouanet prints them, a long melisma on "ni".
N:UNCERTAIN: the last sixteenth of bar 8 (B, measured between A and B); "Ya" in bar 15 (Rouanet's word sits between the c and the B). The tempo is ours ("Allegro").
